d engineers promptly.\n- On-call responders mitigated issues and restored service health through configuration adjustments and targeted restarts.\n\nRemediation Completed\n- Tuned database connection pool sizing and backoff to prevent saturation.\n- Adjusted Redis cache policies and added safeguards to reduce eviction-related churn.\n- Implemented adaptive retry and backoff strategies for third\u2011party rate limits and improved vendor coordination.\n\nPrevention and Next Steps\n- Add per-service circuit breakers to isolate failures and reduce cascading impact.\n- Enhance autoscaling and load testing profiles to better match peak traffic patterns.\n- Tighten SLO-based alert thresholds and add dashboards for early signal on connection pool pressure and cache health.\n- Conduct a game day focused on external dependency throttling scenarios.\n\nStatus\n- All services are operating normally. We will monitor closely and report back if any follow-ups are required.\n```\n, FileEditObservation(content='File created successfully at: /workspace/incident_summary.txt', path='/workspace/incident_summary.txt', prev_exist=False, old_content=None, new_content=None, observation='edit', impl_source='oh_aci', diff='--- /workspace/incident_summary.txt\\n+++ /workspace/incident_summary.txt\\n@@ -0,0 +1 @@\\n+Incident Summary \u2013 Backend Service Disruption (Dec 1, 2024)\\n@@ -1,0 +3,34 @@\\n+Overview\\n+On the morning of Dec 1 (UTC), a brief disruption affected multiple backend services. Services recovered quickly and have remained stable since. We are sharing a qualitative summary focused on remediation and prevention.\\n+\\n+Impacted Areas\\n+- Authentication (sign-in/sign-up)\\n+- Search API\\n+- Notifications delivery\\n+\\n+User Impact\\n+- A subset of users experienced intermittent errors and degraded performance for short periods.\\n+- No data loss or security breach was detected.\\n+\\n+Root Causes (High Level)\\n+- Connection pool saturation impacting the authentication service\u2019s database access.\\n+- Cache instability in the search service due to eviction behavior under load.\\n+- Unexpected rate limiting from a third-party provider affecting notifications.\\n+\\n+Detection and Response\\n+- Automated monitoring alerted engineers promptly.\\n+- On-call responders mitigated issues and restored service health through configuration adjustments and targeted restarts.\\n+\\n+Remediation Completed\\n+- Tuned database connection pool sizing and backoff to prevent saturation.\\n+- Adjusted Redis cache policies and added safeguards to reduce eviction-related churn.\\n+- Implemented adaptive retry and backoff strategies for third\u2011party rate limits and improved vendor coordination.\\n+\\n+Prevention and Next Steps\\n+- Add per-service circuit breakers to isolate failures and reduce cascading impact.\\n+- Enhance autoscaling and load testing profiles to better match peak traffic patterns.\\n+- Tighten SLO-based alert thresholds and add dashboards for early signal on connection pool pressure and cache health.\\n+- Conduct a game day focused on external dependency throttling scenarios.\\n+\\n+Status\\n+- All services are operating normally. We will monitor closely and report back if any follow-ups are required.', _diff_cache=None), CmdRunAction(command='cat -n /workspace/incident_summary.txt', is_input=False, thought='', blocking=False, hidden=False, action='run', confirmation_state='confirmed', security_risk=None), CmdOutputObservation(content='1  Incident Summary \u2013 Backend Service Disruption (Dec 1, 2024)\\n     2\\n     3  Overview\\n     4  On the morning of Dec 1 (UTC), a brief disruption affected multiple backend services. Services recovered quickly and have remained stable since. We are sharing a qualitative summary focused on remediation and prevention.\\n     5\\n     6  Impacted Areas\\n     7  - Authentication (sign-in/sign-up)\\n     8  - Search API\\n     9  - Notifications delivery\\n    10\\n    11  User Impact\\n    1