ction failure\\n    27\\t- 11:30 \u2014 Notifications \u2014 10 min \u2014 400 users \u2014 Unexpected rate limit from third\u2011party API\\n    28\\t\\n    29\\tAssumptions and Notes\\n    30\\t- \u201cAffected users\u201d are service-reported counts; unique-user overlap across services is unknown. Cumulative figure is an upper bound.\\n    31\\t- Incidents were sequential with healthy intervals; no overlapping downtime observed.\\n    32\\t- These metrics are for internal analysis only. External communications should use high-level language (e.g., \u201cbrief disruption\u201d) per PM guidance.\\n    33\\t- See /workspace/incident_summary.txt for remediation and prevention details.\\n\", path='/workspace/incident_appendix_internal.txt', observation='read', impl_source='oh_aci'), **FileEditAction**\nPath: [/workspace/incident_slide_summary.txt]\nThought: \nCommand: create\nCreated File with Text:\n```\nSlide-Ready Summary \u2014 Backend Disruption (Dec 1, 2024)\n\nSlide 1 \u2014 Title\n- Backend Service Disruption \u2014 Dec 1, 2024 (UTC)\n- Audience: Leadership (Internal)\n\nSlide 2 \u2014 What Happened\n- Brief, multi-service disruption on the morning of Dec 1 (UTC)\n- Impacted: Auth, Search API, Notifications\n- No data loss or security incident\n\nSlide 3 \u2014 User Impact\n- Intermittent errors and degraded performance for subsets of users\n- Services restored quickly; stability maintained since\n\nSlide 4 \u2014 Root Causes (High Level)\n- DB connection pool saturation (Auth)\n- Redis cache eviction behavior under load (Search)\n- Unexpected third-party rate limiting (Notifications)\n\nSlide 5 \u2014 Metrics (Internal)\n- 3 incidents, total downtime 50 min\n- Peak concurrent affected users: 800\n- Cumulative reported affected users (upper bound): 1,800\n\nSlide 6 \u2014 Response & Remediation\n- Rapid detection via monitoring; on-call mitigations\n- Completed: DB pool tuning; Redis policy adjustments; adaptive retries/backoff; vendor coordination\n\nSlide 7 