al and external communications, ensures we are well-prepared to tackle any questions or concerns.\\n\\nSince everything is prepared neatly:\\n1. The internal appendix with \u201cKey Takeaways\u201d.\\n2. The slide-ready summary.\\n3. The one-paragraph external note.\\n\\nIf there are no immediate changes needed for the slide summary format, I believe we're all set. Converting it to Google Slides or PowerPoint can always be done if the need arises.\\n\\nThank you for your efficient and comprehensive work on this! Should I notify anyone else or upload these documents somewhere specific, or are we ready to circulate them as needed?\", thought='', action='recall'), MessageAction(content='Great\u2014everything is ready to circulate. Here\u2019s a concise rollout plan and suggested destinations. If you confirm your preferred tools (Drive/SharePoint/Confluence/Notion), I can tailor the uploads/links language.\\n\\nWho to notify\\n- Leadership (internal-only appendix + slides): Exec team, CTO/VP Eng, Head of Product, SRE/Infra leadership, Security, Support leadership.\\n- Broad internal (summary only): Engineering org, Support, Product.\\n- External-facing teams (external note only): Customer Success, Account Management, PR/Comms.\\n\\nWhere to upload\\n- Folder: Incidents/2024-12-01 Backend Disruption/\\n  - Public-internal: incident_summary.txt, incident_slide_summary.txt\\n  - Restricted (leadership-only): incident_appendix_internal.txt\\n- Wiki/Confluence/Notion: Post a page \u201cDec 1 Backend Disruption \u2013 Summary & Next Steps\u201d with:\\n  - Summary content inline\\n  - Slides and appendix as attachments/links (appendix with restricted permissions)\\n- Optional: Create a link in your incident management tracker (e.g., Jira/Incident IO) pointing to the summary and appendix.\\n\\nApproval checkpoints\\n- External note: final sign-off by Huang (PM for external comms).\\n- Technical accuracy: quick thumbs-up from SRE/Incident Commander or Eng lead.\\n- Legal/compliance (if your policy requires it): quick review of the external note.\\n\\nReady-to-send draft snippets\\n- Internal email (leadership)\\n  - Subject: [Internal] Dec 1 backend disruption: summary, metrics, next steps\\n  - Body: Sharing a brief summary and slide-ready overview for today\u2019s review. Metrics and assumptions are in the leadership-only appendix. Links: [slides], [appendix], [summary]. Services are stable; remediation complete; prevention work items scheduled.\\n- Slack post (broader internal)\\n  - \u201cWe\u2019ve posted the qualitative summary of the Dec 1 backend disruption and our next steps. Services are stable. Summary: [link]. For leadership, metrics appendix: [restricted link].\u201d\\n- External note (to CS/AM/Comms)\\n  - Use the content from /workspace/external_note.txt. Include a reminder: \u201cUse as-is; avoid adding figures.\u201d\\n\\nLet me know:\\n- Which repository/drive/wiki to upload to, and any specific folder paths.\\n- The distribution lists (email aliases/Slack channels) you want to use.\\n- Whether you want me to send the notifications or just prepare the messages with links after upload.\\n\\nOnce I have the destination details, I can place the files, set suggested permissions, and share the ready-to-send messages with live links.', image_urls=None, wait_for_response=True, action='message', security_risk=None), MessageAction(content='Please continue working on the task on whatever approach you think is suitable.\\nIf you think you have solved the task, please finish the interaction.\\nIMPORTANT: YOU SHOULD NEVER ASK FOR HUMAN HELP.\\nIf you want to give up, run: <execute_bash> exit </execute_bash>.\\n', image_urls=None, wait_for_response=False, action='message', security_risk=None), RecallAction(recall_type='knowledge', query='Please continue working on the task on whatever approach you think is suitable.\\nIf you think you have solved the task, please finish the interaction.\\nIMPORTANT: YOU SHOULD NEVER ASK FOR HUMAN HELP